# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Alin M. Elena et al. (2025). Machine learned potential for high-throughput phonon calculations of metal—organic frameworks.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-025-01611-8  arXiv:2412.02877v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2412.02877v3 (sha256 5eedc29bbed25526...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 361 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/elena2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the curated PBE-D3(BJ) data set of 127 MOFs (MD
# frames, equation-of-state strains and optimisation trajectories
# selected by farthest-point sampling; 4,764 DFT points, 85/7.5/7.5 %),
# the two multi-head fine-tunes of MACE-MP-0b (MACE-MP-MOF0 with a
# random split, MACE-MP-MOF0-v2 with an FPS split; 2,500 epochs), their
# test RMSDs (Table 3) and the out-of-sample RMSDs on 70 QMOF MOFs
# together with MACE-MP-0b (Table 4). Lattice parameters, phonons, bulk
# moduli and thermal expansion are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-elena2025 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Elena et al. (2025): MACE-MP-MOF0, a fine-tuned MACE-MP-0b for high-throughput phonon calculations of metal-organic frameworks" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-elena2025 .

